cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenFAWE, please cite the paper given as preferred citation and, for the code, this release."
title: "OpenFAWE: an open framework for coupled floating airborne wind energy dynamics and physics-linked cost screening"
abstract: >-
  OpenFAWE is an open-source code for the aerodynamics of airborne wind energy kites, developed towards
  floating airborne wind energy. Release 0.2.0 contains the aerodynamic module (lifting line, vortex step
  method and vortex-lattice lifting surface with straight or time-marching free vortex wakes; NumPy,
  Numba, CPU tree-code and GPU tree-code Biot-Savart backends), actuator-disc rotors that release
  vortex rings into the free wake, prescribed crosswind motions of one or several kites in one vortex
  system, a lumped-mass tether, the TU Delft V3 and Makani M600 models, and the run scripts and data of
  the paper arXiv:2610.37313. Control, ground station, power and floating-platform models are under
  development and are not part of this release.
type: software
